by its Path3D. The line will be generated
automatically.

This pulley leads to fight against
Dr. Eggman himself!
"

[node name="TestStageTutorial2_Enemies" parent="." unique_id=980460116 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-4.37114e-08, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, -4.37114e-08, -230.967, 4, 179.584)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial2_Enemies" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This is a tower with badniks.
They are automatically culled at certain
distance so you can just easily place
them onto level without worrying about
optimization too much. Same goes for
items like rings."

[node name="TestStageTutorial4_EndGoal" parent="." unique_id=424910449 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, -5.96046e-08, 0, 1, 0, 5.96046e-08, 0, -1, -73.0123, 5.20323, -47.92)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial4_EndGoal" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "It all ends here. The end of the stage.
Ranks are controlled through StageData,
but each goal ring can lead into different
stage.

Ensure that StageData matches with
stage data in the main menu!"

[node name="TestStageTutorial5_SpecialStage" parent="." unique_id=2029008334 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, 8.74228e-08, 0, 1, 0, -8.74228e-08, 0, -1, -44.3965, 4.07733, -27.4821)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial5_SpecialStage" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This is an entrance to the Special Stage.
You can collect Chaos Emeralds there.
Or 50 rings if you have them all.

If you have them all,
you can turn into Super Sonic!"

[node name="TestStageTutorial6_MovingPlatform" parent="." unique_id=693828336 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 42.9392, 4, -6.20334)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial6_MovingPlatform" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "Moving platform. It moves along Path3D.

If you can't see it, look up."

[node name="TestStageTutorial7_Automation" parent="." unique_id=378502173 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 117.163, 4, -2.59974)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial7_Automation" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This is an automated path. Its triggers are
hidden in dash pads. Touch them to run
along Path3D.
If you lock input through dash panel,
player won't have to press anything.
Otherwise it will just limit the path of
movement.

Additionally, it's an example of how you
can make roads using CSGPolygon3D."

[node name="TestStageTutorial8_LostWorldGravity" parent="." unique_id=357065219 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-4.37114e-08, 0, -1, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -4.37114e-08, 197.349, 4.43417, 135.633)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial8_LostWorldGravity" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This spring leads to place with Lost World gravity.
Path3D controls the direction of gravity, so
your gravity sasuages can be of any shape.

Everything in Badnik Framework has
been designed with any gravity in mind."

[node name="TestStageTutorial9_FlatGround" parent="." unique_id=521854428 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-1, 0, 8.74228e-08, 0, 1, 0, -8.74228e-08, 0, -1, 27.793, 5, 201.79)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial9_FlatGround" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This is flat terrain. It may not look like it's flat,
but it's flat. Walk on it to sense its flatness.

You can make a collider \"flat\" by setting it's
layer to FlatGround."

[node name="TestStageTutorial10_NoWalkGround" parent="." unique_id=1348230304 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-4.37114e-08, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, -4.37114e-08, -59.9325, 5, 210.901)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial10_NoWalkGround" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "This is an unwalkable collider. You can use it
to ensure player will never walk on it and will just
slide off. It's good for invisible walls.

It's controlled by layer NoWalkGround in the
collider."

[node name="TestStageTutorial11_2D" parent="." unique_id=280738318 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -28.6829, 8.66174, -223.116)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial11_2D" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "2D section ahead!
It's compromised of few elements:
- Curve to define walking plane
- Camera trigger
- Trigger to set movement"

[node name="TestStageTutorial12_EnemiesIn2D" parent="." unique_id=1680831083 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
transform = Transform3D(-4.37114e-08, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, -4.37114e-08, -4.44865, 67.5826, -286.978)

[node name="Label3D" parent="TestStageTutorial12_EnemiesIn2D" index="0" unique_id=284775712]
text = "Enemies are affected by gravity triggers
and 2D triggers just like player.

There's no need to do anything special
in order for them to work in 2D."

[node name="TestStageTutorial13_Water" parent="." unique_id=100219904 instance=ExtResource("59_nd2cx")]
